--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DIAGNOSTIC DECOMPOSITION (labelled variants, NOT frozen cells): the bracket-B
rerun differs from the baseline in TWO ways at once -- (1) the 0.30 dex/dex IMF
mass correction and (2) the added log sigma_e control. But delta contains
+2 log sigma_e ALGEBRAICALLY (M_dyn = K_v sigma^2 Re/G), so at fixed M*,Re the
dynamical 'hotter' signal AND a sigma-correlated IMF BOTH live in the same
log sigma_e direction: the sigma_e control removes signal and confounder
TOGETHER (structural degeneracy of the Stage-1 proxy design). Which piece kills
the slope is decided below by separating them:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  P2 | canon | imfB-corr ONLY (C3)   N=48  slope=-0.5454 (68% [-0.8152,-0.4407]; 95% [-0.9643,-0.1719]) p_MG0=0.022 [zero-OUTSIDE]  partial-Spearman rho=-0.312 [-0.589,+0.030]  resid=0.156  <- IMF correction alone, no sigma control
  P2 | canon | fixedIMF + sig-ctrl (C4) N=48  slope=+0.0005 (68% [-0.0017,+0.0013]; 95% [-0.0111,+0.0033]) p_MG0=0.799 [ZERO-INSIDE]  partial-Spearman rho=+0.068 [-0.297,+0.389]  resid=0.001  <- sigma control alone, no IMF correction
  read-off: the literature-scale (0.30 dex/dex) IMF correction alone moves the
  fixed-IMF slope -0.6355 -> -0.5454 (14% removed); the log sigma_e CONTROL is what
  drives the frozen bracket-B cell to ~0 (it also removes the signal channel).
  A sigma-dependent IMF would need a slope of ~2.0 dex/dex in log sigma to
  cancel the whole fixed-IMF slope through the mass term alone -- ~6-7x the
  literature trend. BUT by the FROZEN standard (FROZEN.md sec.2: 'a slope that
  dies under bracket B is reported as NOT robust'), the MI-like slope is NOT
  ROBUST -- reported verbatim; the degeneracy statement above is the reason the
  frozen standard is this conservative at Stage 1 (sigma_e is simultaneously the
  dynamical thermometer and the IMF proxy; only Stage-2 Jeans beta, which is not
  a monotone function of sigma_e, breaks the degeneracy).

