(iii) resolved-subsample-only vs full-catalog-proxy: EMPTY BY FREEZE -- FROZEN.md
     sec.3 froze NO DAPall-level anisotropy proxy (P1/P2 are MAPS-resolved only),
     so there is no catalog-level regression to compare against. Stated, not run.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACCELERATION-REGIME BUDGET (computed, honesty-critical for reading the sign)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  canon: y = g_bar/a0 median 7.9 (16-84% [5.8,10.9]); log10 nu median 0.0258 dex, 16-84% spread [0.0190,0.0345]
  alt: y = g_bar/a0 median 6.6 (16-84% [4.8,9.0]); log10 nu median 0.0307 dex, 16-84% spread [0.0228,0.0410]
  => the fixed-IMF trend amplitude |slope|*s_P2 = 0.173 dex vs the entire
  MI lever arm (16-84% spread of log nu) = 0.015 dex: the observed trend is
  ~11x larger than the MAXIMUM any genuine MI anisotropy effect could
  be in this high-acceleration sample (these massive ETGs sit at y~5-11 where the
  framework boost nu-1 is only ~2-10%). So even at face value the MI-like sign
  CANNOT be read as MI support -- the amplitude is dominated by structural/
  K_v/sigma-channel systematics, exactly what the firewall anticipated. Stage 2
  must target LOW-y pressure-supported systems (dSphs, dwarf ETGs, cluster
  outskirts) where the MI budget is O(0.02-0.05 dex) and beta is Jeans-measured.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POWER STATEMENT for full-Jeans STAGE 2 (from the observed Stage-1 scatter)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
observed: post-control robust delta scatter s_e = 0.181 dex; P2 spread s_P2 = 0.272; P1 spread 0.051 (N=33).
Stage 2 regresses delta on per-galaxy JAM/Jeans beta_r. Detectable-at-3sigma
(with 80% power, z=3+0.84) sample size: N ~ ((3.84 * s_e) / (b * s_beta_eff))^2,
s_beta_eff = attenuated beta spread s_beta*sqrt(s_beta^2/(s_beta^2+e_beta^2)).
Expected MI slope scale (illustrative, from the rider-a bracket: the isotropic-
ensemble offset bracket spans ~0.02-0.05 dex over the anisotropy range;
mi_closure_pin/CONSEQUENCES.md sec.1 -- 'toy magnitudes illustrative'):
 b [dex/unit beta] | s_beta=0.20 e_beta=0.05 | s_beta=0.20 e_beta=0.10 | s_beta=0.15 e_beta=0.10
              0.02 | N ~   32213           | N ~   37897           | N ~   77853          
              0.05 | N ~    5154           | N ~    6064           | N ~   12457          
              0.10 | N ~    1289           | N ~    1516           | N ~    3114          
MaNGA DR17 supplies ~382 primary slow rotators (2,407 quality parent); ATLAS3D-
style JAM beta_z is published for ~260 ETGs. => Stage 2 at b~0.05 needs s_e
driven DOWN (distances/M*: ~0.10-0.15 dex plausible with SBF/fundamental-plane
distances + resolved M/L) and N~10^2-10^3: FEASIBLE only at the optimistic corner;
at b~0.02 it needs N>~10^3 WITH s_e~0.1 -> requires stacking or a survey beyond
current JAM samples. Honest bottom line printed from the numbers above.

