READ-OFF (computed above, nothing hard-coded): the frozen discriminator cell is
P2|canon|fixedIMF and its bracket-B rerun. MI expects slope<0, MG expects 0.
  P2_canon_fixedIMF           : slope -0.6355 [-1.1406,-0.2002] -> MI-like (<0)
  P2_canon_imfB_sigma-dep     : slope +0.0020 [-0.0107,+0.0056] -> CONSISTENT WITH MG ZERO
  P2_alt_fixedIMF             : slope -0.6358 [-1.1382,-0.1985] -> MI-like (<0)
  P2_alt_imfB_sigma-dep       : slope +0.0024 [-0.0135,+0.0065] -> CONSISTENT WITH MG ZERO
BY THE FROZEN STANDARD (FROZEN.md sec.2): the slope dies under bracket B ->
the MI-like fixed-IMF slope is NOT ROBUST. The diagnostic decomposition shows
the death comes from the log sigma_e CONTROL (which removes the dynamical
signal channel together with the IMF confounder -- structural Stage-1
degeneracy), not from the literature-scale IMF correction itself; both facts
carried at equal prominence.
FIREWALL REMINDER: exploratory; proxy is NOT beta; nothing here supports or
kills the framework. Verdict language above is about THIS PROXY only.
